.TH GIT-ALMANAC 1 "2026-08-29" "git-almanac 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
\&
.PP
git-almanac \- inspect local Git calendars, authors, contributors, and reports
.SH SYNOPSIS
\&
.B git-almanac calendar
.RI [ repository ]
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B git-almanac authors
.RI [ repository ]
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B git-almanac contributors
.RI [ repository ]
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B git-almanac report
.RI [ calendar | authors | contributors ]
.RI [ repository ]
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B git-almanac config
.RI < init | show | check >
.RI [ repository ]
.PP
.B git-almanac ignore
.RI [ repository ]
.PP
.B git-almanac init
.RI [ repository ]
.PP
.B git-almanac completion
.RI < bash | zsh >
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&
.B git-almanac
inspects commits reachable from one local Git ref without network requests
or a forge account.
With no repository argument, it discovers the repository containing the
current directory.
.PP
The default interval contains 365 local calendar dates ending today.
Commits are grouped by author date in the local timezone,
merge commits are excluded,
and exact raw Git
.I Name <email>
identities are preserved.
.SH COMMANDS
\&
.TP
.BR calendar " [" repository "]"
Render selected activity as a terminal, HTML, SVG, or JSON
contribution calendar.
.TP
.BR authors " [" repository "]"
List exact author identities in deterministic identity order
with counts and shares.
.TP
.BR contributors " [" repository "]"
Rank exact identities by selected commit activity and report their shares.
.TP
.BR report " [" calendar | authors | contributors "] [" repository "]"
Build all or one compatible static view under
.IR reports/git-almanac/ .
.TP
.BR config " <" init | show | check "> [" repository "]"
Create, display, or validate optional repository-local defaults.
.TP
.BR ignore " [" repository "]"
Add the narrowest safe report rule to the repository-root
.IR .gitignore .
.TP
.BR init " [" repository "]"
Initialise configuration and report ignore behavior without generating a report.
.TP
.BR completion " <" bash | zsh ">"
Write a sourceable completion definition to standard output.
.SH SHARED HISTORY OPTIONS
\&
.TP
.BI --author " pattern"
Pass an author name or email pattern to Git.
.TP
.BI --path " pathspec"
Restrict history with a Git pathspec relative to the repository root.
This option may be repeated.
.TP
.BI --ref " git-ref"
Select the reachable history root.
The default is HEAD.
.TP
.BI --since " YYYY-MM-DD"
Set the first counted local calendar date.
.TP
.BI --until " YYYY-MM-DD"
Set the last counted local calendar date.
The default is today.
.TP
.BI --date " author|committer"
Choose the Git timestamp grouped into local calendar days.
The default is author.
.TP
.B --include-merges
Include merge commits.
Merges are excluded by default.
.TP
.BI --metric " commits"
Select the counting metric.
Commits is the only current metric.
.TP
.BI --theme " light|dark"
Select the visual palette.
The default is light.
.SH STANDALONE OUTPUT OPTIONS
\&
.TP
.BI --format " terminal|html|svg|json"
Select a renderer.
Authors and contributors do not support SVG.
.TP
.BI --output " path"
Write one exact path instead of standard output.
An HTML, SVG, or JSON extension infers format when
.B --format
is absent.
.TP
.BI --output-dir " path"
With
.BR calendar ,
write one combined file and one deterministic file for every
exact author identity.
.TP
.B --no-color
Disable ANSI terminal color.
.PP
An explicit format overrides output-extension inference.
A format without an output path writes to standard output.
.SH OTHER OPTIONS
\&
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Show command help and exit successfully.
.TP
.BR \-V , " \-\-version"
Show the Git Almanac version and exit successfully.
.SH REPORT WORKSPACE
\&
.PP
Reports live under
.IR <repository-root>/reports/git-almanac/ .
The workspace contains linked HTML pages, normalized JSON data,
a combined SVG calendar,
per-contributor SVG calendars, and
.IR manifest.json .
.PP
The manifest records the effective repository, revision, history selectors,
timezone,
identity policy, metric, theme, sections, and managed paths.
A complete report automatically rebuilds every managed section when that
contract changes, removes stale managed files, and preserves unowned files.
A named partial update requires a compatible contract.
Git Almanac refuses a non-empty directory without a valid manifest,
unsafe managed paths, and collisions with unowned paths.
.SH CONFIGURATION
\&
.PP
Optional
.I <repository-root>/.git-almanac.toml
uses schema 1.
Built-in defaults apply first, repository configuration second,
and CLI arguments last.
Supported keys are ref, since, until, date, include_merges, metric,
theme, author, and paths.
.PP
.B config init
does not replace an existing configuration.
.B ignore
uses
.I /reports/
only when no tracked or foreign report content could be hidden;
otherwise it uses
.IR /reports/git-almanac/ .
.SH COUNTING CONTRACT
\&
.PP
Each commit object reachable from the selected ref is counted at most once.
All authors are included unless filtered.
Exact raw author identities remain separate.
Merge inclusion, date field, timezone grouping, ref, date interval,
and pathspecs are explicit in JSON and report manifests.
.PP
Contributor percentages describe selected commit activity
and are not productivity scores.
.SH OUTPUTS
\&
.PP
Terminal output preserves five distinguishable intensity states without color.
HTML is self-contained and embeds an accessible SVG.
Standalone SVG cells carry keyboard focus, date and count labels,
and native hover details.
JSON models use schemaVersion 1.
.SH FILES
\&
.TP
.I <repository-root>/.git-almanac.toml
Optional repository-local defaults.
.TP
.I <repository-root>/reports/git-almanac/
Managed static report workspace.
.TP
.I <repository-root>/.gitignore
Modified only by explicit ignore or init commands.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
\&
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable terminal ANSI color when the variable is present.
.TP
.B TZ
Select the process timezone through standard runtime handling.
.TP
.B GIT_ALMANAC_INSTALL_DIR
Override the installer executable directory.
.TP
.B GIT_ALMANAC_MAN_INSTALL_DIR
Override the installer manual directory.
.TP
.B GIT_ALMANAC_VERSION
Select the exact v-prefixed release for install.sh.
.SH INSTALLATION
\&
.PP
Install an immutable released asset with:
.nf
curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/knowledgeislands/tools-git-almanac/\
main/install.sh | bash
.fi
.PP
For local development, run:
.nf
\&./install.sh --link
git almanac calendar
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
\&
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Repository, Git, configuration, report ownership, rendering, or output failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid git-almanac syntax or option value.
.SH SEE ALSO
\&
.BR git (1),
.BR git-log (1),
.BR gitignore (5)
